{
  "_comment": "Shared writer/reader parity fixtures for the subject/header parity invariant. Each case pins a raw commit MESSAGE (the body after the git header/message split) and the subject + GitMsg header line that BOTH the Go writer (subjectOf / extractHeaderLine in site_items.go) and the JS reader (cleanContent + first line / parseGitmsg in gs-core.js) must derive from it identically. rawObject cases additionally pin the full loose-object commit text so the header/message split parity (gpgsig blocks, CRLF) is covered end to end. feedbackCards pins the review verdict and the file:line anchor label both renderers put on a feedback card. releaseHeads pins the subject and the version chip both renderers put on a release head. detailHeads pins the subject and the head chips both renderers put on a detail head. rowHeads pins the same for a list or activity row, whose tinted glyph carries the state its head chip would repeat. metaRow pins the meta row skeleton: the bit classes in order, the same row once the item is edited, and the author label and its email title both renderers derive. defaultTitles pins the name both renderers give a site with no configured title. listEmpty pins each list route\u0027s empty sentence, which both renderers show. rowGlyphs pins the type glyph class and title both renderers give a row, the extension default standing in for a header that names no type. releaseRows pins the asset count both renderers put on a release row in place of its hash. releaseNotes pins the blocks a release body splits into, so the commit rows and their hashes read the same on both surfaces, and releaseAssets pins the artifact, checksum and SBOM rows and which of them carry a link. markdownPaths pins the extensions both renderers render as prose and mdxStrip the MDX lines both drop before parsing. cardSkeleton pins the one card shape: the part order and the head slot order both renderers build, per item type, and the headless shape a body-only type takes, where the marker leads the meta row and the first line stands as the card's text. frontFiles pins the cap on the front page's root listing and the control label both renderers show once it hides entries.",
  "messageCases": [
    {
      "name": "gpgsig-message-body",
      "message": "Fix the widget layout\n\nThe grid collapsed on narrow screens; this pins the min-width.\n\nGitMsg: ext=\"pm\" v=\"1\" type=\"issue\" state=\"closed\"",
      "expectSubject": "Fix the widget layout",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"pm\" v=\"1\" type=\"issue\" state=\"closed\""
    },
    {
      "name": "crlf-line-endings",
      "message": "Ship release v2.1\r\n\r\nHighlights:\r\n- faster search\r\n\r\nGitMsg: ext=\"release\" v=\"1\" type=\"release\" tag=\"v2.1\"",
      "expectSubject": "Ship release v2.1",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"release\" v=\"1\" type=\"release\" tag=\"v2.1\""
    },
    {
      "name": "body-starts-with-gitmsg-empty-subject",
      "message": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "no-header",
      "message": "Plain commit with no trailer\n\nJust a body.",
      "expectSubject": "Plain commit with no trailer",
      "expectHeader": ""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: heading",
      "message": "# Shipping the reader\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "Shipping the reader",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: emphasis",
      "message": "**Shipping v2** and _soon_\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "Shipping v2 and soon",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: link",
      "message": "See [the notes](https://example.com/x) now\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "See the notes now",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: image",
      "message": "![a logo](logo.png) ships\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "a logo ships",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: inline code",
      "message": "Use `gitsocial push` first\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "Use gitsocial push first",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: plain already",
      "message": "Nothing to strip here\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "Nothing to strip here",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: inline html",
      "message": "<b>_bold_</b> ships\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "bold ships",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: html wrapping a heading",
      "message": "<p># Title</p>\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "Title",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: link beside html emphasis",
      "message": "[x](y) <em>_z_</em>\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "x z",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    },
    {
      "name": "subject strip: markup only",
      "message": "<br/>\n\nbody\nGitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\"",
      "expectSubject": "",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"social\" v=\"1\" type=\"post\""
    }
  ],
  "rawObjectCases": [
    {
      "name": "gpgsig-raw-object",
      "commitText": "tree 4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904\nparent 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111\nauthor Ada <ada@example.com> 1700000000 +0000\ncommitter Ada <ada@example.com> 1700000000 +0000\ngpgsig -----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n \n iQIzBAABCgAdFiEExampleKeyFingerprintForTestingPurposesOnly1234567890\n AAoJEExampleSignatureBytesThatSpanMultipleContinuationLinesWith\n BlankContinuationLinesInThePgpArmorBlockToExerciseTheHeaderSplit\n -----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nSign the important thing\n\nBody after a signed header block.\n\nGitMsg: ext=\"review\" v=\"1\" type=\"pull-request\" state=\"open\"",
      "expectSubject": "Sign the important thing",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"review\" v=\"1\" type=\"pull-request\" state=\"open\""
    },
    {
      "name": "crlf-raw-object",
      "commitText": "tree 4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904\nauthor Bob <bob@example.com> 1700000100 +0000\ncommitter Bob <bob@example.com> 1700000100 +0000\n\nWindows checkout\r\n\r\nEdited on a CRLF machine.\r\n\r\nGitMsg: ext=\"memo\" v=\"1\" type=\"memo\"",
      "expectSubject": "Windows checkout",
      "expectHeader": "GitMsg: ext=\"memo\" v=\"1\" type=\"memo\""
    }
  ],
